WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.142 --> 00:00:02.044
The Saudi bank failed to rule

00:00:02.044 --> 00:00:04.046
out giving funding to the

00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:05.614
already embattled company that

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:07.616
combined with the recent U.S.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:08.817
Issue sent stocks falling.

00:00:09.017 --> 00:00:13.088
I want to bring in business

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:15.323
reporter rahel Solomon, rahel,

00:00:15.457 --> 00:00:16.858
walk us through what happened

00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:17.325
today.

00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:18.894
&gt;&gt; Well, Jake, basically the

00:00:19.027 --> 00:00:22.531
mood for investors, as investors

00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:24.699
search for the next sign of

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:25.434
weakness.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.070
To be clear, I think the NASDAQ

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.004
actually closed slightly higher

00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:30.405
which is interesting.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:32.140
But this is really just a

00:00:32.274 --> 00:00:33.375
confidence issue at this point.

00:00:33.508 --> 00:00:35.343
You can see that reflected very

00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:37.012
clearly in some of the bank

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:37.345
stocks.

00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:38.480
I want to point your attention

00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:40.415
to some of the regional stocks,

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:42.084
Jake, you and I have talked

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.552
about already.

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:48.323
First republic bank off 21%,

00:00:48.457 --> 00:00:51.159
pac-west off 5% on top of the

00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:51.493
losses.

00:00:51.626 --> 00:00:53.395
It's been a rough go for some of

00:00:53.528 --> 00:00:55.130
the regional stocks as we face

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.032
the confidence issue in banking.

00:00:57.165 --> 00:01:00.102
But some of the larger banks

00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:02.104
getting swept up in the selloff.

00:01:02.104 --> 00:01:06.708
Chase was off earlier bank of

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:10.112
America, citigroup, Wells Fargo

00:01:10.145 --> 00:01:16.384
getting caught up in the larger.

00:01:16.518 --> 00:01:18.120
And Chase Bank it's been

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.454
considered the problem child of

00:01:19.588 --> 00:01:22.124
European banking, so it had its

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:25.360
fair share of issues even before

00:01:25.494 --> 00:01:26.761
svb's collapse and signature.

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:28.930
I think what we're witnessing

00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:30.699
how on edge investors are about

00:01:30.832 --> 00:01:33.168
the sector and banking outlook

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:35.203
and really confidence issues

00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:36.204
moving forward.

00:01:36.338 --> 00:01:39.207
&gt;&gt; The situation regulator just

00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:40.342
put out a statement trying to

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:42.244
shore up confidence in credit

00:01:42.377 --> 00:01:42.577
Suisse.

00:01:42.711 --> 00:01:43.612
What did they say?

00:01:43.745 --> 00:01:44.579
And might that work?

00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:46.148
&gt;&gt; Well that is the big

00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:47.115
question, right, this comment,

00:01:47.249 --> 00:01:49.751
this statement coming out about

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:51.353
30 minutes ago from Swiss

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:57.692
regulators essentially from the

00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:00.428
smb and the signature bank,

00:02:00.562 --> 00:02:02.664
I.e., svb do not pose a risk for

00:02:02.797 --> 00:02:05.333
the financial markets.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.434
Here's what's perhaps most

00:02:06.568 --> 00:02:08.170
important, Jake.

00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:12.174
Credit Suisse meets the requires

00:02:12.174 --> 00:02:15.477
on requirements imposed, it

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.811
looks called but the most

00:02:16.945 --> 00:02:17.345
important thing.

00:02:17.479 --> 00:02:20.515
If necessary, the Swiss bank

00:02:20.649 --> 00:02:22.184
will provide with liquidity.

00:02:22.184 --> 00:02:24.186
You're getting assurances there

00:02:24.186 --> 00:02:25.086
with the national bank much like

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:26.955
we saw with the federal reserve.

00:02:27.088 --> 00:02:28.757
&gt;&gt; Rahal, thank you for that.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.194
Phil Mattingly joins us live.

00:02:32.227 --> 00:02:35.197
Phil, you've been speaking to

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.198
officials at the U.S.

00:02:36.198 --> 00:02:36.798
Treasuretry department.

00:02:36.932 --> 00:02:38.200
What's their plan?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.202
&gt;&gt; What rahel just read off

00:02:40.202 --> 00:02:41.436
track what is officials are

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.204
trying to make clear throughout

00:02:42.337 --> 00:02:43.505
the course of this day.

00:02:43.638 --> 00:02:44.439
And that is the fact what

00:02:44.573 --> 00:02:46.208
happened over the weekend with

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:46.608
silicon valley bank, with

00:02:46.741 --> 00:02:47.809
signature bank, the problems

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.212
that we've seen with regional

00:02:50.345 --> 00:02:52.214
banks are not necessarily

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.216
connected to what is happening

00:02:54.316 --> 00:02:56.751
with Credit Suisse.

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:58.220
But they're positive with the

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.222
fact that there has been a mood

00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:01.623
shift in how people are viewing

00:03:01.756 --> 00:03:03.592
the sector, therefore any

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:05.427
problem can create a risk

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.629
particularly in one in a bank as

00:03:07.762 --> 00:03:09.497
large as Credit Suisse.

00:03:09.631 --> 00:03:11.466
So U.S. Officials have been

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.500
monitoring through Credit Suisse

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:13.735
throughout the course of the

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:14.236
day.

00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:16.504
They've been talking on a pretty

00:03:16.638 --> 00:03:17.706
regular basis with their

00:03:17.839 --> 00:03:19.241
counterparts in Europe as well

00:03:19.374 --> 00:03:21.042
trying to make sure that the

00:03:21.176 --> 00:03:22.410
spillover risk is limited.

00:03:22.544 --> 00:03:27.549
And if there is spillover risk,

00:03:27.682 --> 00:03:29.551
they're cognizant of that fact.

00:03:29.684 --> 00:03:31.720
Try to make clear, these are

00:03:31.853 --> 00:03:33.688
separate issues, but, Jake, a

00:03:33.822 --> 00:03:35.023
general sense of the market of

00:03:35.156 --> 00:03:36.925
the anxiety, and they need to be

00:03:37.058 --> 00:03:38.260
prepared for anything that may

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:38.593
come next.

00:03:38.727 --> 00:03:41.196
&gt;&gt; Phil, has all of this had

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:42.430
officials question whether they

00:03:42.564 --> 00:03:44.499
did enough three days ago from

00:03:44.633 --> 00:03:46.268
stop this from exacerbating?

00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:48.336
&gt;&gt; Well, what's interesting, in

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:48.937
conversations I've had

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.272
throughout the day, the short

00:03:50.272 --> 00:03:50.905
answer is, no.

00:03:51.039 --> 00:03:52.807
The tools they put in place,

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:56.444
both back stopping the uninsured

00:03:56.578 --> 00:04:01.483
deposits, well as the insured

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.485
deposits at the two banks.

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:05.020
And to other lenders that may

00:04:05.153 --> 00:04:06.821
fail as well.

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:12.627
Trying to ensure confidence in

00:04:12.761 --> 00:04:13.928
depositors, over the course of

00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:16.298
the last through days that, they

00:04:16.298 --> 00:04:18.333
feel, has started to take hold.

00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:20.502
The limited facility they've set

00:04:20.635 --> 00:04:22.304
up at the federal reserve has

00:04:22.304 --> 00:04:24.306
created options for lines of

00:04:24.306 --> 00:04:25.907
banks most stressed at this

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:26.341
point.

00:04:26.341 --> 00:04:28.310
They feel those were the right

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:28.443
tools.

00:04:28.576 --> 00:04:30.378
It's worth noting they were very

00:04:30.512 --> 00:04:31.079
significant emergency

00:04:31.212 --> 00:04:33.014
interventions put on the table.

00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:34.883
And what's happening with credit

00:04:35.016 --> 00:04:36.384
Suisse right now doesn't change

00:04:36.518 --> 00:04:37.619
their view that those are the

00:04:37.752 --> 00:04:38.853
right answers.

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.388
I do believe, in talking to

00:04:40.522 --> 00:04:42.724
these officials, again, as we've

00:04:42.857 --> 00:04:44.326
been discussing, they are

00:04:44.326 --> 00:04:45.193
cognizant of the fact that the

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:46.494
real problem they face at this

00:04:46.628 --> 00:04:48.697
moment in time is perception, is

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.064
panic.

00:04:49.197 --> 00:04:50.832
People's perception of risk, as

00:04:50.965 --> 00:04:52.434
this continues to play out, even

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:53.868
if they don't think necessarily

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:55.737
these institutions are

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:56.905
connected, these particular

00:04:57.038 --> 00:04:58.340
problems are connected.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.741
If the view becomes that the

00:04:59.874 --> 00:05:01.543
system is unstable, that it

00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:02.811
doesn't matter what capital bank

00:05:02.944 --> 00:05:03.978
is holding or what the

00:05:04.346 --> 00:05:05.213
regulations are in place, then

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:06.881
they have very big problems that

00:05:07.015 --> 00:05:08.350
can spread very quickly.

00:05:08.383 --> 00:05:09.884
If you look at the equities

00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:11.519
markets, Jake, and you look at

00:05:11.653 --> 00:05:14.356
the biggest banks taking a hit

00:05:14.356 --> 00:05:16.725
right now, JPMorgan or bank of

00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:18.793
America, on the equity side,

00:05:18.927 --> 00:05:20.362
that does not track with how

00:05:20.362 --> 00:05:21.363
everything is going over the

00:05:21.496 --> 00:05:24.366
last several days.

00:05:24.466 --> 00:05:28.770
Most of the major deposits have

00:05:28.903 --> 00:05:30.905
been going to the banks.

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:32.374
They feel they're substantial

00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:33.842
and yet, they've taken a hit.

00:05:33.975 --> 00:05:35.076
All of this drives to the idea

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.544
that there's a shifting in the

00:05:36.678 --> 00:05:37.579
marketplace right now.

00:05:37.712 --> 00:05:39.781
A very real concern about risks,

00:05:39.914 --> 00:05:41.983
a very real concern about

00:05:42.384 --> 00:05:44.419
constagen and spillover effects.

00:05:44.552 --> 00:05:45.920
They feel what will they've put

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:47.489
in place can manage what they're

00:05:47.622 --> 00:05:48.590
dealing with at home.

00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:50.759
But they know things can spread.

00:05:50.892 --> 00:05:52.394
And very aware of that fact and

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.762
I think prepared for that fact

00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:55.029
as well, Jake.

00:05:55.163 --> 00:05:59.234
&gt;&gt; Presumably, Phil, the

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:00.402
administration is discussing

00:06:00.402 --> 00:06:01.569
whether or not congress should

00:06:01.703 --> 00:06:03.338
step in and legislate, tell us

00:06:03.471 --> 00:06:03.972
about that.

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:05.206
&gt;&gt; When you talk to

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.408
administration officials they

00:06:06.408 --> 00:06:08.610
say two things when it comes to

00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:10.412
the regulatory side and whether

00:06:10.412 --> 00:06:11.413
or not they'd need emergency

00:06:11.546 --> 00:06:12.547
action from capitol hill.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.416
One, the president has talked

00:06:14.416 --> 00:06:15.316
about regulation and perhaps

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.819
putting back in place the 2018

00:06:17.952 --> 00:06:20.422
regulations that were eased on

00:06:20.422 --> 00:06:22.023
smaller banks under president

00:06:22.424 --> 00:06:22.490
trump.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:23.958
That is something that does not

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:27.729
seem to have any pathway forward

00:06:27.862 --> 00:06:28.797
nor any immediate effect of what

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.865
we're watching and dealing with

00:06:30.999 --> 00:06:32.434
now, when it comes to capitol

00:06:32.467 --> 00:06:33.435
hill with emergency infusion of

00:06:33.568 --> 00:06:35.036
cash there aren't a lot of

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.638
conversations, in part because

00:06:36.771 --> 00:06:38.773
it's a recognition of a

00:06:38.907 --> 00:06:40.842
political environment and

00:06:40.975 --> 00:06:41.543
government where Republicans

00:06:41.676 --> 00:06:42.544
have stated opposition what

00:06:42.677 --> 00:06:44.446
happened over the weekend.

00:06:44.446 --> 00:06:46.681
Almost all of whom are deeply

00:06:46.815 --> 00:06:48.917
opposed to what happened back in

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:49.217
2008.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.718
So there's no real move to doing

00:06:50.852 --> 00:06:51.653
something like that.

00:06:51.786 --> 00:06:53.421
Plus, they don't think that's

00:06:53.555 --> 00:06:54.456
necessitated at this point in

00:06:54.556 --> 00:06:56.458
time based on what they're

00:06:56.458 --> 00:06:56.491
seeing.

